    "q-113850": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113850",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the antiderivative of \n$\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}-x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}-x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{4/5}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int {x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/5+1}}{(\\frac{4}{5}+1)}-\\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{(1+1)}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/5}}{(\\frac{9}{5})}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2}{3{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-113850-a",
